  "id": "effort-syndrome",
  "term": "effort syndrome",
  "definition": "Effort syndrome is a condition in which even slight physical exertion leads to symptoms such as palpitations, shortness of breath, labored breathing, and a sense of discomfort or strain. It can also involve dizziness, shakiness, sweating, and insomnia, and is commonly viewed as a form of anxiety disorder.",
